From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 18:20:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: keep an IOKit string's terminator inside its buffer

cf_to_string copied up to buffer_size bytes of a CFData property and then
wrote the terminating NUL at buffer[length]: a property of buffer_size
bytes or more (128 for the platform expert's manufacturer and model) wrote
one byte past the caller's array. It now copies at most buffer_size - 1
bytes. Nothing shows the iPhone's properties reach that length, so it is
not known to touch Red Dead Redemption 2's launcher (PLA-401); a host
test reproduced the overflow while checking the SMBIOS table it reads.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-18-rockstar-smbios-conformance.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c
index 087a1c0..4871960 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/system.c
@@ -2413,7 +2413,7 @@ static void cf_to_string( CFTypeRef type_ref, char *buffer, size_t buffer_size )
 
     if (CFGetTypeID(type_ref) == CFDataGetTypeID())
     {
-        size_t length = MIN(CFDataGetLength(type_ref), buffer_size);
+        size_t length = MIN(CFDataGetLength(type_ref), buffer_size - 1);
         CFDataGetBytes(type_ref, CFRangeMake(0, length), (UInt8*)buffer);
         buffer[length] = 0;
     }
